  70: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  71:     """
  72:     Recolor the row-wise passage indicated by wall pixels with the singleton marker color.
  73: 
  74:     Input structure:
  75:     - A dominant background contains one singleton marker pixel and one wall color.
  76:     - Wall pixels lie on several rows and form left/right limits around the marker column.
  77:     - Empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows are open horizontal passages.
  78: 
  79:     Rule:
  80:     - On a wall row, paint background pixels between the nearest wall strictly
  81:       left of the marker column and the nearest wall at or right of it; if only
  82:       one side is present, paint from that wall to the opposite grid edge.
  83:     - On empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows, paint the whole row.
  84:     - On empty rows outside the wall-row band, reuse the nearest end wall-row interval.
  85:     - Preserve wall pixels and the original marker pixel.
  86: 
  87:     Key insight:
  88:     - The wall color defines scanline limits relative to the marker column; the
  89:       marker color fills those implied horizontal spans rather than flood-filling
  90:       through connected background.
